00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:23,379
A scout is brave.

250
00:19:23,719 --> 00:19:23,899
Yep.

251
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,719
A scout can face danger.

252
00:19:26,139 --> 00:19:28,199
He might be afraid, but he can still face it.

253
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:33,399
He has the courage to stand for what he thinks is right, even if others laugh at him or threaten

254
00:19:33,399 --> 00:19:33,719
him.

255
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,360
That's real bravery in my book.

256
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:42,780
Chutzpah is a great old Yiddish word that has been defined as a combination of gall and

257
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:47,500
nerve and guts and presumption and arrogance.

258
00:19:48,199 --> 00:19:54,760
I mean, it might not be as noble as the connotations that we attach to bravery.

259
00:19:55,280 --> 00:20:01,520
And it may not be that all brave people have chutzpah, but those with chutzpah, baby, they are

260
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,199
brave in one way or another.

261
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:07,060
I mean, it takes real chutzpah to stand up to society.

262
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:13,880
Our Scouts win popularity or risk ostracism at the shifting standards of their peers.

263
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:16,020
Do you remember that?

264
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:16,460
Remember?

265
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:21,020
One day, one thing was cool and you go to school the next day and it's not cool anymore.

266
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:30,900
There's no more unforgiving and intense and capricious society than the one we encounter

267
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,360
when we're teenagers, you know.

268
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:40,000
It takes chutzpah to be a scout in that society, to stand out and to achieve in a world that

269
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,260
often belittles anyone who dares to explore their own potential.

270
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:47,280
But we've got chutzpah, right?

271
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,980
Because a scout is brave.

